TECHNICAL CORRECTNESS FIXES
12. 0.1 step 2: "glcycle_t emits a zone for every clock" contradicted the no-per-draw-zones rule: drawcalls is clocked in every Apply() (vk_renderstate.cpp:183), SetupWall/Flat/Sprite per job (hw_bsp.cpp:149,188,197). Now: zones only for named per-scene clocks. Added API fact: Tracy zones must nest LIFO per thread; assert it.
13. F2: new trap 4. PortalBlocksMovement depends on PLANEF_NOPASS|DISABLED|OBSTRUCTED|LINKED (g_levellocals.h:934-937), and CheckPortalPlane flips OBSTRUCTED when a plane passes the portal (p_sectors.cpp:983-992), with no actor movement. The key now includes both planes' portal flags. "linePortalEpoch" -> level-wide portalEpoch covering line portals/UpdatePortal (portal.cpp:240)/polyobj portal lines/sector-portal assignment. "Three traps" -> "Five traps".
14. F2: the conservative rule "skip early-out when Sector has a non-blocking portal plane" left a stale list when a portal turns blocking; added "or touching_sectorportallist is non-empty".
15. F3: "reset mLastMaterial when a new command buffer begins (FlushCommands)" -> reset in EndRenderPass (vk_renderstate.cpp:490-504), which every flush goes through (vk_commandbuffer.cpp:136). BeginRenderPass forces mChanged=true (577), so a key compare without the reset would skip the first bind in a new command buffer.
16. F3 set-0 rule: also rebind after a new command buffer; added the API fact on pipeline-layout compatibility.
17. F7: made the change concrete: the pointer comes from GetBuffer() via a separate load of mCurIndex before fetch_add. Fix: index = fetch_add; return {GetBuffer(index), index}.
18. F10: the pole test "pitch ± vfov/2 crosses ±90°" is wrong with head roll -> "±Z inside all four side planes". Added why min/max corner yaw is exact.
19. F10 / Phase 2 step 4 contradiction: "Phase 2 feeds FrustumAngle the combined stereo frustum". The angular clippers are centred on each eye (dual clipper), while the combined frustum's apex sits behind the midpoint. Its yaw range under-covers near geometry seen from an eye, so it is not conservative. Now: each eye clipper uses its own eye frustum; the combined frustum feeds only the item cull and the GPU cull.
20. F12: "replace the spin with a sleep until 0.5 ms before the deadline" would not recover the measured 2.3 ms. The wait is a fixed pad equal to the last tic's run time (TicStabilityBegin/End, 2124-2135), so the padding itself is the cost. Rewritten: off under OpenXR, default off on desktop with a judder check, smoothed TicFrac as the fix if needed, sleep+spin only saves power.
21. Phase 2 step 6: the sketch called SetStereoViews before SetupView, but SetupView rebuilds mViewMatrix, recomputes the normal matrix and uploads (hw_drawinfo.cpp:425-433), so it would overwrite the per-view matrices. Added the required ordering and change.
22. Phase 3 C occlusion: "clipper from both capsule ends, shrink by 2·asin(r/d)" is not conservative between the ends. A running player moves 16-23 units/tic against r ≈ 3-4 units. Replaced with sample points at spacing s, each tested with radius ρ = sqrt(r² + (s/2)²) (ρ = r√2 at s = 2r; a first draft of this fix used r, which leaves gaps at r√2). Cull only when all samples agree. Alternative: one midpoint clipper with R = r + L/2.
23. Phase 4 step 5: "fragment shader picks the first plane below the fragment" selects the wrong band. Now: entry i with plane[i] ≥ z > plane[i+1], matching uSplitTopPlane/uSplitBottomPlane in hw_walls.cpp:293-320 (last band's low plane = sector floor).

